{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01RsGbCHAa6pRJXKttnPVmYs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Anchor â€” what it is, grounded in the project docs:**\n\n- **A single-folder personal productivity system** for J.C. Liechty, living entirely in `C:\\dev\\Anchor` (no OneDrive, no siblings, no syncing). The source of truth is plain markdown files â€” `DASHBOARD.md`, `PROJECTS.md`, `INBOX.md`, domain files (`domains/academic.md`, `commercial.md`, etc.), plus archives like `CANCELLED.md` and `SAVED_FOR_LATER.md`.\n\n- **It ships a local web app (`anchor_gui.py`)** â€” a self-contained Python-stdlib HTTP server that renders an interactive browser dashboard at `http://localhost:8777` and writes changes straight back to the markdown. It runs persistently as the NSSM Windows service `anchor` (not launched by hand). A CLI engine (`anchor.py`) mirrors the same logic and generates a static `dashboard.html`.\n\n- **Core task-management surface:** tasks move through a lifecycle (Active â†’ Done â†’ Cancelled â†’ Saved-for-Later â†’ Restored) with priority/energy/domain/due/notes fields, captured via dashboard or CLI commands (`done:`, `add:`, `capture:`, etc.).\n\n- **A reliability layer:** `anchor_healthcheck.py` runs daily at 5 AM via Task Scheduler, parsing every file, booting a throwaway test server, exercising all endpoints and state transitions (and the v2/v3/v4 R&D surfaces, fully stubbed), then writing dated reports to `health_reports/`.\n\n- **Its largest evolving feature is the R&D Control Surface (now v4 \"Project Cockpit,\" built + merged to master 2026-06-13).** This turns each project into a mission-control cockpit for the **trio workflow â€” researchPrime (Research) â†’ Crucible (Planning) â†’ Foreman (Build)**. Per the locked North Star, each lane shows its most-recent session as a **tile with one honest status light** (green/amber/red/grey); clicking expands an **inline panel** (balanced summary on top, a real resizable terminal below) rather than navigating away.\n\n- **What the R&D surface technically ships:** real **ConPTY terminals** (the one declared native exception, `pywinpty`, lazy-loaded in `pty_manager.py` only), **per-session git-worktree isolation**, durable session/registry persistence under `.anchor/`, an **engine toggle** (Claudeâ†”Gemini, Gemini research-only), cached+validated session/project summaries, a Grass-Catchers idea board with promote-to-lane, type-aware deliverable launching, stage handoffs, ephemeral deliverable previews (hard-guarded never to bind 8777), and Ghost World Labs branding.\n\n- **Hard architectural rules:** Python stdlib only (the lone `pywinpty` exception aside, enforced by `distro.py`'s import scan); markdown remains the source of truth (no DB, no lock files); all files stay plain-text and accessible from any CLI tool.\n\nOne caveat on grounding: these claims come from `CLAUDE.md` and the embedded North Star/locked-decision excerpts (the docs themselves), not from re-reading every module â€” but the file structure and module roles described are consistent across the CLAUDE.md sections."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4410,"cache_read_input_tokens":45306,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4410,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fa4611af-0cbf-460e-aa23-41692e8221d7","uuid":"13282ffd-35b2-49ff-ae3a-025af440a697","request_id":"req_011Cc1hYQLS4jnHmMScaQTQT"}
